Package: faperu
Title: Access and Design-Based Analysis of Peruvian Official Surveys and Censuses
Version: 0.4.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Fred", "Torres Cruz", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0834-6834")),
    person("Richar Andre", "Vilca Solorzano", email = "andrevilcasolorzano@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0003-2385-5263"))
  )
Description: Downloads, reads and analyses ten official statistical
    sources of Peru from a single catalog: the National Household Survey
    (ENAHO), the Demographic and Family Health Survey (ENDES), the National
    Agricultural Survey (ENA), the Permanent National Employment Survey
    (EPEN), the National Survey of Budget Programmes (ENAPRES), the National
    Time Use Survey (ENUT), the National Survey on Social Relations (ENARES)
    and the Annual Economic Survey, all from the National Institute of
    Statistics and Informatics (INEI)
    <https://proyectos.inei.gob.pe/microdatos/>, together with the School
    Census of the Ministry of Education (MINEDU) and the 2017 National
    Censuses. Files are cached and verified with SHA-256, only the requested
    columns are read, and district codes are harmonised to the 2017 census
    frame. Survey designs follow INEI's technical documentation and are
    passed to the 'survey' package (Lumley, 2004
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v009.i08>), giving means, proportions and totals with
    standard errors, confidence intervals and INEI's coefficient-of-variation
    quality bands. Seven ready indicators reproduce INEI's published
    figures, and estimates from different surveys can be linked by
    department or district and shown as tables or maps. The package is
    independent of INEI and MINEDU.
